# Commercial S7 previous-release upgrade-source diagnosis

- Observed at: 2026-08-30T11:01:00Z
- Scope: fresh S7 preflight after the credential-release refresh
- Result: fail-closed before application sync, service start, or Nginx change

## Symptom

The fresh preflight stopped with `APPLICATION_RELEASE_UNEXPECTED`.

## Evidence

The server application was clean at the exact prior S7 release:

- commit: `3dd63f7a17626a4d8a8a3b58f317ae6917c33696`
- tree: `e247b749ffa155a5ab8ea884ff77d205d5762dd7`

That release had been installed during the earlier authorized attempt before the
runtime credential guard triggered the automatic service/Nginx rollback. It is
neither drift nor an unreviewed state. Control and application worktrees remained
clean, and the newly created pre-deployment backup verified successfully.

## Resolution

Add this one exact commit/tree pair as a permitted upgrade source. The controller
may fast-forward it only to the newly reviewed target:

- target commit: `79a9d88d51ba5747cdfb0b6400a61506d82ccc6b`
- target tree: `f3ae60f4c690a3b023db4e5953ca14050a9272b3`

All other application states remain rejected. Fast-forward-only synchronization,
remote target equality, clean worktree, source hashes, backup, and preflight
requirements remain mandatory.

## Rollback

Revert this commit and keep S7 disabled. The change contains no runtime or server
activation and grants no wildcard or branch-based release acceptance.
